  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Community Recovery: Ensuring Conducive Economic and Agriculture Environments in Sumska oblast</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Ukrainian economy, already affected by the COVID-19 pandemic, faces serious recovery challenges due to the war in Ukraine following Russia&apos;s invasion in February 2022.Humanitarian assistance remains critical to address the serious needs associated with the ongoing conflict, but targeted action is also needed to promote economic resilience, early recovery, durable solutions including local integration, and prevent communities from falling back into humanitarian dependency. In response to these challenges, IOM proposes a comprehensive socio-economic recovery response that aims to strengthen the livelihoods of affected populations and communities to support economic recovery and development in Ukraine, using a holistic framework encompassing interventions at the individual, community and systems levels.</narrative>
  </description>
